{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low-bias: model systematically underestimates the level, especially from ~day 10 onward; apply an upward level shift that increases with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger in days 10–30).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: during sustained rallies the model reacts too slowly (forecasts stay near low/mid-60s while realized moves into high-60s); add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 day slope to lift the whole path.",
    "Underestimation grows with horizon: errors are modest early but widen materially by weeks 3–4; use horizon-dependent scaling (e.g., add a linear ramp or multiply deviations from last price by >1 for days 15–30).",
    "Peaks are capped too low: the model misses upside spikes/upper tail (realized highs ~69–70 vs forecasts ~66–68); increase volatility/upper-quantile allowance when recent realized volatility is elevated.",
    "Mean reversion too strong: forecasts revert back toward ~63–66 even when the regime has shifted upward; reduce mean-reversion strength when price breaks above recent 20–30d range or when consecutive higher closes occur."
  ]
}
